An allocation of a process holds its region slots to the build's budget rather than the entries the PMP has,
so on RP2350's Hazard3, with seven, a process may have more regions installed than its image has entries for.

Caught-by: fuzz-rp2350
Report: process has no region slot, or more than the hardware has entries
Witness: fuzz-rp2350 process-region-slots

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -384,7 +384,7 @@ static int op_pool(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
         }
         /* A region slot for each region it may have installed at once, one at least and an entry each at most. */
         uint32_t regions = arg[4];
-        if (regions == 0 || regions > pmp_entry_count) {
+        if (regions == 0 || regions > PMP_MAX_ENTRIES) {
             return KERR_INVALID_ARG;
         }
         struct process *proc = pool_alloc(pool, CAP_PROCESS, obj_type_size(CAP_PROCESS, regions));
